{"id":"economics-p007","bookId":"economics","number":7,"title":"七、经济名词","width":1190.55,"height":841.89,"image":"data/knowledge/pages/economics/economics-p007.svg","dataUrl":"data/knowledge/pages/economics/economics-p007.json","questionCount":14,"version":1,"imagePixels":[2084,1474],"source":{"file":"27上岸村·经济常识思维导图.pdf","sha256":"3d065db3e8c49c841592240a1c627f823daa5e9f906824196a5a6fc9cb35c7e3","page":7},"nodes":[{"id":"economics-p007-n0001","text":"七、经济名词","bbox":[80.555,400.715,124.284,20.714],"color":"#141414","fontSize":20.714,"block":0,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0002","text":"黑天鹅事件","bbox":[307.067,100.086,92.062,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":1,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0003","text":"极其罕见、难以预测，但一旦发生就会产生颠覆性影响的小概率事件","bbox":[442.859,100.086,552.375,18.412],"color":"#8e24aa","fontSize":18.412,"block":1,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0004","text":"灰犀牛事件","bbox":[307.067,184.093,92.062,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":2,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0005","text":"明显的、高概率的、早已存在，但却被人们有意或无意忽视，","bbox":[442.859,156.474,497.137,18.412],"color":"#ff6f00","fontSize":18.412,"block":3,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0006","text":"最终可能酿成重大危机的事件","bbox":[442.859,184.093,239.362,18.412],"color":"#ff6f00","fontSize":18.412,"block":3,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0007","text":"流动性偏好","bbox":[307.067,268.1,92.062,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":4,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0008","text":"人们在心理上更偏好持有现金或能快速变现的资产，","bbox":[442.859,240.481,423.487,18.412],"color":"#1e88e5","fontSize":18.412,"block":5,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0009","text":"而非收益较高但难以快速、无损失变现的资产的倾向","bbox":[442.859,268.1,423.487,18.412],"color":"#1e88e5","fontSize":18.412,"block":5,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0010","text":"流动性陷阱","bbox":[307.067,379.725,92.062,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":6,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0011","text":"当利率降至零或接近零的极低水平时，人们宁愿以现金或储蓄的形式持有货币，","bbox":[442.859,324.488,644.437,18.412],"color":"#19a719","fontSize":18.412,"block":7,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0012","text":"而不愿进行投资或消费，导致中央银行通过增加货币供应量、降低利率来刺激经","bbox":[442.859,352.107,644.437,18.412],"color":"#19a719","fontSize":18.412,"block":8,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0013","text":"济的货币政策完全无效的状态","bbox":[442.859,379.725,239.362,18.412],"color":"#19a719","fontSize":18.412,"block":8,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0014","text":"边际效用递减","bbox":[307.067,463.732,110.475,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":9,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0015","text":"在一定时间内，在其他商品的消费数量保持不变的条件下，当一个人连续消费某种","bbox":[461.271,436.114,662.849,18.412],"color":"#ce4289","fontSize":18.412,"block":10,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0016","text":"物品时，随着所消费的该物品的数量增加，其所带来的效用的增加量有递减的趋势","bbox":[461.271,463.732,662.849,18.412],"color":"#ce4289","fontSize":18.412,"block":10,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0017","text":"拉弗曲线","bbox":[307.067,547.739,73.65,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":11,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0018","text":"当税率在一定的限度以下时，提高税率能增加政府税收收入","bbox":[424.446,520.12,478.725,18.412],"color":"#0096bf","fontSize":18.412,"block":12,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0019","text":"但超过这一限度时，再提高税率反而导致政府税收收入减少","bbox":[424.446,547.739,478.725,18.412],"color":"#0096bf","fontSize":18.412,"block":12,"line":1,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0020","text":"公共物品","bbox":[307.067,657.063,73.65,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":13,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0021","text":"满足社会公众需要的商品。一般具有两大特征","bbox":[424.446,604.127,368.25,18.412],"color":"#141414","fontSize":18.412,"block":14,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0022","text":"①非竞争性：消费者对某种物品的消费并不会影响其他人对该物品的消费","bbox":[424.446,657.063,589.199,18.412],"color":"#3949ab","fontSize":18.412,"block":15,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0023","text":"②非排他性：消费者对某种物品的消费并不会阻止其他人对该物品的消费","bbox":[424.446,709.999,589.199,18.412],"color":"#3949ab","fontSize":18.412,"block":16,"line":0,"emphasis":true,"role":"content"},{"id":"economics-p007-n0024","text":"7","bbox":[591.275,810.711,8.0,21.344],"color":"#000000","fontSize":16.0,"block":17,"line":0,"emphasis":false,"role":"page-number"}],"blocks":[{"id":"economics-p007-b0001","text":"七、经济名词","bbox":[80.555,400.715,124.284,20.714],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0001"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0002","text":"黑天鹅事件极其罕见、难以预测，但一旦发生就会产生颠覆性影响的小概率事件","bbox":[307.067,100.086,688.167,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0002","economics-p007-n0003"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0003","text":"灰犀牛事件","bbox":[307.067,184.093,92.062,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0004"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0004","text":"明显的、高概率的、早已存在，但却被人们有意或无意忽视，最终可能酿成重大危机的事件","bbox":[442.859,156.474,497.137,46.031],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0005","economics-p007-n0006"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0005","text":"流动性偏好","bbox":[307.067,268.1,92.062,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0007"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0006","text":"人们在心理上更偏好持有现金或能快速变现的资产，而非收益较高但难以快速、无损失变现的资产的倾向","bbox":[442.859,240.481,423.487,46.031],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0008","economics-p007-n0009"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0007","text":"流动性陷阱","bbox":[307.067,379.725,92.062,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0010"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0008","text":"当利率降至零或接近零的极低水平时，人们宁愿以现金或储蓄的形式持有货币，","bbox":[442.859,324.488,644.437,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0011"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0009","text":"而不愿进行投资或消费，导致中央银行通过增加货币供应量、降低利率来刺激经济的货币政策完全无效的状态","bbox":[442.859,352.107,644.437,46.03],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0012","economics-p007-n0013"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0010","text":"边际效用递减","bbox":[307.067,463.732,110.475,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0014"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0011","text":"在一定时间内，在其他商品的消费数量保持不变的条件下，当一个人连续消费某种物品时，随着所消费的该物品的数量增加，其所带来的效用的增加量有递减的趋势","bbox":[461.271,436.114,662.849,46.03],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0015","economics-p007-n0016"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0012","text":"拉弗曲线","bbox":[307.067,547.739,73.65,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0017"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0013","text":"当税率在一定的限度以下时，提高税率能增加政府税收收入但超过这一限度时，再提高税率反而导致政府税收收入减少","bbox":[424.446,520.12,478.725,46.031],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0018","economics-p007-n0019"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0014","text":"公共物品","bbox":[307.067,657.063,73.65,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0020"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0015","text":"满足社会公众需要的商品。一般具有两大特征","bbox":[424.446,604.127,368.25,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0021"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0016","text":"①非竞争性：消费者对某种物品的消费并不会影响其他人对该物品的消费","bbox":[424.446,657.063,589.199,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0022"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0017","text":"②非排他性：消费者对某种物品的消费并不会阻止其他人对该物品的消费","bbox":[424.446,709.999,589.199,18.412],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0023"]},{"id":"economics-p007-b0018","text":"7","bbox":[591.275,810.711,8.0,21.344],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0024"]}],"questions":[{"id":"economics-p007-q001","number":1,"type":"fill-in","answer":"极其罕见、难以预测，但一旦发生就会产生颠覆性影响的小概率事件","bbox":[442.859,100.086,552.375,18.412],"fontSize":18.412,"color":"#8e24aa","segments":[{"text":"极其罕见、难以预测，但一旦发生就会产生颠覆性影响的小概率事件","bbox":[442.859,100.086,552.375,18.412],"color":"#8e24aa"}],"nodeIds":["economics-p007-n0003"],"aliases":[],"context":"黑天鹅事件____"},{"id":"economics-p007-q002","number":2,"type":"fill-in","answer":"明显的、高概率的、早已存在